{"reference":"Psalms 106","book":"Psalms","chapter":106,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Book Boundary","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 106 closes with a blessing and communal “Amen” (v. 48). In the Masoretic arrangement of the Psalter, this verse is understood as a doxological boundary marking the end of the fourth of its five books.","verse_refs":["Psalms 106:48"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_106_306e1677eeacc24a4bfc569c"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}